Track 3: The Migrant’s Molt
- Story & Context: Now a local legend of the underground, they say the traveler finally finished their transformation during a blackout at the terminus, leaving only a pile of discarded conductive fabric on the seat as the city woke up. Witnesses claim the tunnels hum with a new, permanent melody now, as if the rails themselves have learned to weep for those who keep moving. "I have left the weight of the city behind," rings out as a haunting, polyphonic synth-chorus that mimics the sound of a thousand iron needles dropping.
